			<div class="content" id="post-content-1963927">
									

<p>I had downvoted this article a while ago, mostly because I don't really care for MC&amp;D as a hook, but re-reading this right now made me change my mind.</p>
<p>I like how it's a sex offender's vacation dream house, but I would really like to see some logs shedding a little (just a wee bit) of light on the workings of SCP-102-2. I like vague SCPs that make you finish the story in your own mind, but I'm drawing a complete blank about the second house.</p>
<p>The only thing I can think of is, that since the first one makes you incorporeal so you can go outside and easily rape people, the second one, somehow makes it easier for the occupant to be raped. That would explain the psychological trauma and the need for steroids to enhance the damaged musculature from being held still for an extended amount of time. Maybe ghostly figures hold you and mollest you for the duration of the lease, or something like that.</p>
<p>I know it's been a while, but am I close to what you intended here, Yoric?</p>
<p>Anyway, it's very creepy in how it's an anomalous object tailored to fulfill horrible sexual fantasies, regardless of MC&amp;D. So I upvoted it this time.</p>

